1. Command pattern is a behavioural design pattern, that turn request into a object.
- Command pattern = Encapsulate a request to object

2. Real world analogy
- Think of a remote control
- Button = command
- Remote = invoker
- TV/AC = receiver

3. Without command pattern
- if (button == "ON") tv.turnOn();
  else if (button == "OFF") tv.turnOff();
- Tight coupling
- Hard to extend
- No undo / redo

4. Structure of command pattern
- Command (Interface)
- Concrete Command
- Receiver (Actual Logic )
- Invoker (Triggers Command)

5. In real flutter these patterns can be used to handle button
clicks (diff logic , sign up )

6. Use command pattern when
- You  need tpo undo / redo
- You want to queue the task
- You want to decouple sender/ receiver

7. Main difference between command pattern and strategy pattern
- Strategy Pattern => Choose how to do , Focuses on algorithm,
Switch behaviour
- Command Pattern => Choose what to do, focus is 'Request', Trigger action






